+## Sales import and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO 8601 instant with a zone,
+  `qty` a whole number of portions). Each row uses one recipe portion per
+  `qty` from stock, with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>` and the time
+  `soldAt`. Rows of a ticket imported before are skipped. It answers
+  `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 3 }`: the tickets and the rows (dish lines)
+  imported. If a row is not valid (`bad_request`) or an item runs out
+  (`sale_not_enough_stock`), nothing from the file is imported and the
+  message names the row; `row 2` is the first data row.
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one
+  `{ "itemId", "theoretical", "actual", "difference" }` per item, for the days
+  `from` to `to` inclusive (UTC): `theoretical` is what the sales sold in those
+  days use by recipe, `actual` is every `consume` movement in those days, and
+  `difference` is `actual` minus `theoretical`. Items where both are zero are
+  left out.
